{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-93098" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the root of $f(x)=-5\\sqrt[4]{3x+1}+10.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004556/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb7b50b929b9bb28b0ce642d20fe1f63e306437158aaa21bcf55081fa627832"} {"question" "q-93098" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n-5\\sqrt[4]{3x+1}+10=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5\\sqrt[4]{3x+1}+10 & =0 \\\\ -5\\sqrt[4]{3x+1} & =-10 \\\\ \\sqrt[4]{3x+1} & =2 \\\\ (\\sqrt[4]{3x+1})^{4} & ={2}^{4} \\\\ 3x+1 & =16 \\\\ 3x & =15 \\\\ x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we must check the answer by substituting it back into the initial equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5\\sqrt[4]{3\\cdot 5+1}+10 & =0 \\\\ -5\\sqrt[4]{16}+10 & =0 \\\\ -5\\cdot 2+10 & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004556/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb7b50b929b9bb28b0ce642d20fe1f63e306437158aaa21bcf55081fa627832"} {"question" "q-93098" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004556/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "014f28db02d93e0049ee90bbff450b488ed6bda61064b3f2e801b6612200684b"} {"question" "q-93098" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004556/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb7b50b929b9bb28b0ce642d20fe1f63e306437158aaa21bcf55081fa627832"} {"question" "q-93098" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-4"] ["math" "x=5"] ["math" "x=\\frac{17}{3}"] ["math" "x=\\pm 3"] ["text" "The function has no root"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004556/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb7b50b929b9bb28b0ce642d20fe1f63e306437158aaa21bcf55081fa627832"} {"question" "q-93098" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004556/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb7b50b929b9bb28b0ce642d20fe1f63e306437158aaa21bcf55081fa627832"} {"question" "q-93099" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the root of $f(x)=-4\\sqrt[6]{5x-11}-8.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004556/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb7b50b929b9bb28b0ce642d20fe1f63e306437158aaa21bcf55081fa627832"} {"question" "q-93099" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n-4\\sqrt[6]{5x-11}-8=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4\\sqrt[6]{5x-11}-8 & =0 \\\\ -4\\sqrt[6]{5x-11} & =8 \\\\ \\sqrt[6]{5x-11} & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any solutions since its left-hand side is always nonnegative, while the right-hand side is negative.\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has no root." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004556/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb7b50b929b9bb28b0ce642d20fe1f63e306437158aaa21bcf55081fa627832"} {"question" "q-93099" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004556/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "014f28db02d93e0049ee90bbff450b488ed6bda61064b3f2e801b6612200684b"} {"question" "q-93099" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004556/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb7b50b929b9bb28b0ce642d20fe1f63e306437158aaa21bcf55081fa627832"} {"question" "q-93099" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-15"] ["math" "x=15"] ["math" "x=8"] ["math" "x=\\pm 13"] ["text" "The function has no root"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004556/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb7b50b929b9bb28b0ce642d20fe1f63e306437158aaa21bcf55081fa627832"} {"question" "q-93099" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "The function has no root"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004556/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb7b50b929b9bb28b0ce642d20fe1f63e306437158aaa21bcf55081fa627832"} {"question" "q-270380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the root of $f(x)=2\\sqrt[5]{7-6x}+6.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004556/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb7b50b929b9bb28b0ce642d20fe1f63e306437158aaa21bcf55081fa627832"} {"question" "q-270380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the root of $f(x),$ we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n2\\sqrt[5]{7-6x}+6=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt[5]{7-6x}+6 & =0 \\\\ 2\\sqrt[5]{7-6x} & =-6 \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{7-6x} & =-3 \\\\ (\\sqrt[5]{7-6x})^{5} & =(-3)^{5} \\\\ 7-6x & =-243 \\\\ -6x & =-250 \\\\ x & =\\frac{125}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=\\frac{125}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004556/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb7b50b929b9bb28b0ce642d20fe1f63e306437158aaa21bcf55081fa627832"} {"question" "q-270380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004556/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "014f28db02d93e0049ee90bbff450b488ed6bda61064b3f2e801b6612200684b"} {"question" "q-270380" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004556/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb7b50b929b9bb28b0ce642d20fe1f63e306437158aaa21bcf55081fa627832"} {"question" "q-270380" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{125}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004556/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb7b50b929b9bb28b0ce642d20fe1f63e306437158aaa21bcf55081fa627832"} {"question" "q-277244" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the root of $f(x)=9\\sqrt[7]{2x-6}-9.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004556/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb7b50b929b9bb28b0ce642d20fe1f63e306437158aaa21bcf55081fa627832"} {"question" "q-277244" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the root of $f(x),$ we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n9\\sqrt[7]{2x-6}-9=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9\\sqrt[7]{2x-6}-9 & =0 \\\\ 9\\sqrt[7]{2x-6} & =9 \\\\ \\sqrt[7]{2x-6} & =1 \\\\ (\\sqrt[7]{2x-6})^{7} & ={1}^{7} \\\\ 2x-6 & =1 \\\\ 2x & =7 \\\\ x & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=\\frac{7}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004556/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb7b50b929b9bb28b0ce642d20fe1f63e306437158aaa21bcf55081fa627832"} {"question" "q-277244" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004556/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "014f28db02d93e0049ee90bbff450b488ed6bda61064b3f2e801b6612200684b"} {"question" "q-277244" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004556/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb7b50b929b9bb28b0ce642d20fe1f63e306437158aaa21bcf55081fa627832"} {"question" "q-277244" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004556/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb7b50b929b9bb28b0ce642d20fe1f63e306437158aaa21bcf55081fa627832"} {"question" "q-277256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the root of $f(x)=-5\\sqrt[8]{4x+9}+5.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004556/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb7b50b929b9bb28b0ce642d20fe1f63e306437158aaa21bcf55081fa627832"} {"question" "q-277256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the roots of $f(x),$ we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n-5\\sqrt[8]{4x+9}+5=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5\\sqrt[8]{4x+9}+5 & =0 \\\\ -5\\sqrt[8]{4x+9} & =-5 \\\\ \\sqrt[8]{4x+9} & =1 \\\\ {(\\sqrt[8]{4x+9})}^{8} & ={1}^{8} \\\\ 4x+9 & =1 \\\\ 4x & =-8 \\\\ x & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we must check the answer by substituting it back into the initial equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5\\sqrt[8]{4\\cdot (-2)+9}+5 & =0 \\\\ -5\\sqrt[8]{1}+5 & =0 \\\\ -5\\cdot 1+5 & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004556/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb7b50b929b9bb28b0ce642d20fe1f63e306437158aaa21bcf55081fa627832"} {"question" "q-277256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004556/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "014f28db02d93e0049ee90bbff450b488ed6bda61064b3f2e801b6612200684b"} {"question" "q-277256" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004556/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb7b50b929b9bb28b0ce642d20fe1f63e306437158aaa21bcf55081fa627832"} {"question" "q-277256" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004556/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb7b50b929b9bb28b0ce642d20fe1f63e306437158aaa21bcf55081fa627832"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1098 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
